# FES — Fractal Execute Structure
# Authority: CSA-sealed
# Layer: Engine → Executor → Module

## 1. Canonical Three-Layer Model

```text
Runtime Component
│
├── Engine (Actor)
│     Authority + Capability + Identity + Lifecycle + RAC Endpoint
│     Examples: text-ractor, file-ractor, uri-ractor, image-ractor
│
├── Addon (Capacity Extension)
│     Adapter, Plugin, Bridge, Driver, Provider, Connector, Fixer, Widget
│
├── Executor (Engine Part)
│     Input → Process → Output (IPO)
│     No Authority, No Identity, No Lifecycle, No RAC URI
│     Examples: executor-py, patch-executor, diff-executor, scheduler-executor
│
└── Library / Module (Pure Algorithm)
      rope, myers-diff, utf8, line-index, ast
```

## 2. Layer Properties

### Engine (Actor) — Runtime Authority
```yaml
properties:
  - Authority
  - Capability
  - Identity
  - Lifecycle
  - RAC Endpoint
  - Receipt
  - Telemetry
  - Memory
  - Transaction
  - Contract
can_run_independently: true
```

### Executor (Engine Part) — IPO Processor / MCV Controller
```yaml
properties:
  - Input
  - Process
  - Output
properties_absent:
  - Authority
  - Identity
  - Lifecycle
  - RAC URI
can_run_independently: false
runs_via: "RAC call through Actor"
rac_router_role: "MCV Controller"  # M=Capor/Racor Model, C=IPO Controller, V=SIO View
```

### Module (Atomic Capability) — Capability Implementation
```yaml
properties:
  - Single responsibility
  - IPO compliant
composition: "Executor composes Modules"
```

### Library (Pure Algorithm) — Technical Component
```yaml
properties:
  - No runtime participation
  - Used by Executor/Module/Addon
```

## 3. IPO Model (Mandatory Control-Flow Contract)

```yaml
ipo:
  input:
    - "normalize SIO envelope"
    - "validate RAC URI"
    - "resolve ExecutionContext"
  process:
    - "Capor (WHAT): capability resolution"
    - "Racor (HOW/WHERE): transport + routing"
    - "execute domain operation"
  output:
    - "finalize SIO envelope"
    - "seal FEH + ALR"
    - "dispatch forward"
```

## 4. Naming Grammar (Lexical Boundary = Runtime Discriminator)

```yaml
naming_grammar:
  actor:
    pattern: "^[a-z0-9]+(?:[/-][a-z0-9]+)*$"
    examples: ["text-ractor", "actor/text-ractor", "provider/poolside/laguna"]
    semantics: "namespace/hierarchy"
    separators: ["/", "-"]
  
  executor:
    pattern: "^[a-z0-9]+(?:[/-][a-z0-9]+)*$"
    examples: ["executor-py", "text/patch-executor"]
    semantics: "namespace/hierarchy"
    separators: ["/", "-"]
  
  action:
    pattern: "^[a-z0-9]+(?:[_.-][a-z0-9]+)*$"
    examples: ["text.read", "file.write", "stream.sse", "tool_call.execute"]
    semantics: "capability/action qualification"
    separators: ["_", ".", "-"]
  
  feature:
    pattern: "^[a-z0-9]+(?:[_.-][a-z0-9]+)*$"
    examples: ["snake_case", "camelCase", "stream_sse_decode"]
    semantics: "capability/action qualification"
    separators: ["_", ".", "-"]
```

**Key Principle**: URI grammar ≠ Action/Feature grammar. The difference creates a lexical boundary for runtime type discrimination.

## 5. FES DNA Types (Canonical Contract)

```yaml
fes_dna:
  FesLayer:
    values: [ENGINE, EXECUTOR, MODULE]
    description: "Layer classification in FES model"
  
  EnginePart:
    fields: [uri, name, layer, parent_uri, dna]
    description: "Base descriptor for Executor or Module"
  
  ExecutorDNA:
    fields: [trait, struct, features, bindings, lion_machine, rion_machine, sio_stream]
    description: "Executor canonical definition (trait + struct + features)"
  
  ActorExecutorMapping:
    fields: [actor_uri, actor_name, executor_uri, executor_name, modules, mode]
    description: "Actor → Executor mapping contract"
```

## 6. Machine Binding

```yaml
machine_binding:
  hace-lion-machine:
    transports: [FDI, FFI, Wasm, Pipe, SharedMem]
    mode: "local native"
    runtime: "same-process / in-device"
  
  hace-rion-machine:
    transports: [HTTP, gRPC, WebSocket, RION]
    mode: "remote native"
    runtime: "network / cross-process"
  
  hace-sio-stream:
    transports: [FPI, SSE, WebSocket]
    mode: "streaming"
    runtime: "async generator"
```

